{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>He stood</b> — the land of Canaan was measured and divided among the tribes." "And the meaning: every place upon which His eye was set immediately dissolved, and this is \"the nations were shattered.\"" "<b>They burst asunder</b> — the meaning is that every place over which the Glory passed would burst asunder, or it is by way of parable, that He passed over the kings whom terror seized." "<b>Bowed down</b> — the hills before them, and they became level ground, and pathways everlasting."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:13.481357242Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}